  "title": "Two-Step Multiplication and Subtraction Word Problems",
  "intro": "Help your student use an intermediate product in a two-step problem.",
  "html": "<h2>Teaching notes for parents and teachers</h2><h3>How to teach it</h3><p>Draw the equal groups and find their total. Then show the amount used and subtract it from that total.</p><h3>Example to work through together</h3><p>Use the model below as you explain the example. Have your student point to the quantities as you discuss them.</p><div class=\"model two-step-pencil-model\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Three boxes of four pencils, with seven pencils used\" style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Twelve pencil counters in three groups of four; seven crossed out, five left\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 175\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;min-width:540px\"><title>Find the total, then remove seven once</title><rect class=\"pencil-group\" x=\"15\" y=\"30\" width=\"150\" height=\"85\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#426e6d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#164f5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\">Box 1: 4</text><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"45\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M33 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M63 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"105\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M93 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"135\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M123 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect class=\"pencil-group\" x=\"195\" y=\"30\" width=\"150\" height=\"85\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#426e6d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#164f5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\">Box 2: 4</text><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"225\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M213 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"255\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M243 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"285\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><path class=\"used-pencil\" d=\"M273 60l24 24m0 -24l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c01823\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"315\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><rect class=\"pencil-group\" x=\"375\" y=\"30\" width=\"150\" height=\"85\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"white\" stroke=\"#426e6d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#164f5b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\">Box 3: 4</text><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"405\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"435\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"465\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/><circle class=\"pencil-counter\" cx=\"495\" cy=\"72\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#176e5c\"/></svg><p>Each dot stands for one pencil. Count 12 at first. Cross out seven across the collection, leaving five. The seven used pencils are not seven from each box.</p></div><div class=\"model\"><p class=\"sample-equation\">3 × 4 = 12</p><p>There were 12 pencils altogether.</p><p class=\"sample-equation\">12 − 7 = 5</p><p>Five pencils remain after seven are used.</p></div><h3>Ask your student</h3><blockquote><p>What does our multiplication answer tell us before we subtract?</p></blockquote><h3>If your student needs help</h3><p>If the student subtracts from one group only, outline the full collection represented by the product.</p>",
